abstract:
Observations of neutral-current $\ensuremath{
u}$ interactions on deuterium in the Sudbury Neutrino Observatory are reported. Using the neutral current (NC), elastic scattering, and charged current reactions and assuming the standard ${}^{8}\mathrm{B}$ shape, the ${\ensuremath{
u}}_{e}$ component of the ${}^{8}\mathrm{B}$ solar flux is ${\ensuremath{\varphi}}_{e}{\phantom{ule{0ex}{0ex}}=\phantom{ule{0ex}{0ex}}1.76}_{\ensuremath{-}0.05}^{+0.05}(\mathrm{stat}{)}_{\ensuremath{-}0.09}^{+0.09}(\mathrm{syst})\ifmmode	imes\else	exttimes i{}{10}^{6}\phantom{ule{0ex}{0ex}}{\mathrm{cm}}^{\ensuremath{-}2}{\mathrm{s}}^{\ensuremath{-}1}$ for a kinetic energy threshold of 5 MeV. The non- ${\ensuremath{
u}}_{e}$ component is ${\ensuremath{\varphi}}_{\ensuremath{\mu}\ensuremath{	au}}{\phantom{ule{0ex}{0ex}}=\phantom{ule{0ex}{0ex}}3.41}_{\ensuremath{-}0.45}^{+0.45}(\mathrm{stat}{)}_{\ensuremath{-}0.45}^{+0.48}(\mathrm{syst})\ifmmode	imes\else	exttimes i{}{10}^{6}\phantom{ule{0ex}{0ex}}{\mathrm{cm}}^{\ensuremath{-}2}{\mathrm{s}}^{\ensuremath{-}1}$, $5.3\ensuremath{\sigma}$ greater than zero, providing strong evidence for solar ${\ensuremath{
u}}_{e}$ flavor transformation. The total flux measured with the NC reaction is ${\ensuremath{\varphi}}_{\mathrm{NC}}{\phantom{ule{0ex}{0ex}}=\phantom{ule{0ex}{0ex}}5.09}_{\ensuremath{-}0.43}^{+0.44}(\mathrm{stat}{)}_{\ensuremath{-}0.43}^{+0.46}(\mathrm{syst})\ifmmode	imes\else	exttimes i{}{10}^{6}\phantom{ule{0ex}{0ex}}{\mathrm{cm}}^{\ensuremath{-}2}{\mathrm{s}}^{\ensuremath{-}1}$, consistent with solar models.
